Below is a complete frontend + backend web app using Node.js + Express + simple JSON file storage for persistence (so you can deploy and use immediately). The app allows:

- Creating tasks
- Expanding tasks to show contacts
- Adding contacts per task
- Opening a contact detail modal to log calls, notes, progress updates
- Viewing communication logs per contact
- Updating contact progress status

---

### Project structure

```
/project-root
  /public
    index.html
    style.css
    app.js
  /data
    data.json          <-- stores all tasks, contacts, logs
  server.js            <-- Node.js + Express backend
  package.json
  package-lock.json
```

---

### 1. Backend: `server.js`

- Simple REST API
- Stores all data in `data/data.json` as:
```json
{
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "task-1",
      "name": "Task name",
      "contacts": [
        {
          "id": "contact-1",
          "name": "Contact name",
          "progress": "Initial",
          "logs": [
            {
              "timestamp": 1680000000000,
              "type": "call",
              "note": "Called and discussed X"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

- Supports:
  - GET `/api/tasks` - get all tasks with contacts and logs
  - POST `/api/tasks` - create new task `{name}`
  - POST `/api/tasks/:taskId/contacts` - add new contact `{name}`
  - POST `/api/tasks/:taskId/contacts/:contactId/logs` - add log `{type, note}`
  - PATCH `/api/tasks/:taskId/contacts/:contactId/progress` - update progress `{progress}`

---

### 2. Frontend: `public/index.html`, `public/style.css`, `public/app.js`

- Dashboard with task list
- Expandable tasks showing contacts
- Add task form
- Add contact form per task
- Click contact opens modal to show logs, add logs, update progress

